From 0a5943aa95f189d63054f7a6fef8d46e45995de9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordi Posthumus <jordi.posthumus@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:11:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): escape the literal image token in text instead of
 400

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
The image token in the prompt comes only from image content blocks. Its
literal spelling typed into request text is ordinary text, and the hosted
DeepSeek API passes it through. _normalize_messages instead rejected the
spelling with a ValueError in string content, text parts and reasoning,
for every role. Any replayed conversation that had ever echoed the
spelling -- a tool result quoting it (including an issue report about
this behaviour), a user message, or the model's own reasoning while
discussing it -- therefore 400'd every subsequent request of the session
and killed it; the history is then permanently poisoned. spark-ds41f
issue #1031.

Escape the spelling to IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_TEXT, the ordinary-text spelling,
which is in no added-token vocabulary, before anything is rendered; the
recursive walk covers string content, text parts, reasoning and
tool-call arguments, for every role. Image parts still flatten to
IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER after the escape, and the control-spellings pass
leaves the placeholder alone as before.

Quality:
Requests without the spelling are byte-identical (the escape is a no-op
and adds one container rebuild per message, as the existing deepcopy
already does one). Real image requests render the placeholder exactly as
before, so the reference encoder fixtures are unchanged.

Tests:
- tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41.py: the test that asserted the
  rejection (test_image_token_in_text_is_a_request_error) is replaced by
  test_image_token_in_text_is_escaped_text (string content, all three
  roles) and test_image_token_in_text_parts_and_reasoning_is_escaped_text
  (text part alongside a real image part, tool-call arguments, the
  current turn's reasoning). Runs in the 1107 release test bundle
  (tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41.py is a gate file) and in CI's
  bin/spark build prepare --only vllm series re-application.

Upstream status: fix for spark-ds41f issue #1031; local to this recipe's
series (the tokenizer file is recipe code on the LIL integration branch).
